# Vendored third-party code is compared byte-for-byte against what
# scripts/vendor-n3.mjs builds (tests/vendor-drift.test.ts). Git's autocrlf would
# rewrite line endings on checkout, so a Windows clone would hold a CRLF bundle
# where the script writes LF — the drift test would fail there and pass on Linux
# CI, and `scripts/copy-vendor.mjs` would publish whichever bytes the builder
# happened to have. `-text` turns the conversion off for this directory only.
src/vendor/** -text
